    "done_when": "§11's fix item 2 (stat-gated snapshots) has not landed. In reckon/crew/recovery.py, _watch_snapshot calls classify_pointer for every live pointer on every poll, re-reading the manifest and the run's records. The incremental stream reader and the admission scan bound (merged at c5ac4c4db) took the producer from 24.5 to 6.25 per cent of a core on a nine-run shape, but an unchanged run still costs more than a stat, on GPFS. The node implements the item as the section states it. A run whose pointer, manifest, stream and exit-record mtime and size are all unchanged reuses its previous snapshot. Only the time-derived fields (quiet seconds and stall) are recomputed, from the stat. A change to any of those files, or a process liveness change the snapshot reports, recomputes it. tests/test_an_unchanged_run_costs_one_stat.py drives the producer's snapshot path over runs whose files are unchanged across polls. It counts reads of each file (by patching or by an injected reader) and asserts that an unchanged run's poll opens no file, only stats it. It also asserts that a manifest rewrite, a stream append and an exit record each recompute that run's snapshot, and that the yielded transitions match the full-recompute path over the same sequence. The declared negative control is executed and logged. Base and head arms of tests/test_producer_reads_only_what_changed.py, tests/test_producer_holds_a_lease.py and every other test file that calls watch_ticker or _watch_snapshot (found by grep at the base) show zero added failures, each run with -n 8, each log naming its revision and ending in its pytest summary and EXIT= line.",
    "estimated_hours": 0.9,
    "goal": "A producer poll over a run whose files are unchanged reuses its previous snapshot after one stat per file",
